<title>USA: U.S. WEEKLY SOYBEAN CRUSH - NOPA.</title>
<headline>U.S. WEEKLY SOYBEAN CRUSH - NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 08/06/97    07/30/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 23,549,000  23,577,000    23,242,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  36,558	75,152	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,804,000  35,804,000-R  33,990,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,996,842  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised from 35,451,000.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   08/06/97    07/30/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,904,000   4,649,000     3,939,000</p>
<p> Ind,Ky,Ohio,Mich 4,237,000   3,844,000     3,762,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,304,000   3,619,000     3,490,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,113,000   2,573,000     2,741,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,220,000   2,844,000     3,295,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,012,000   4,732,000     4,064,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,759,000   1,316,000     1,951,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	23,549,000  23,577,000    23,242,000</p>
